EXT. SALT FLATS, ABANDONED RADIO STATION - DAWN

Cracked white earth. A rusted mast. Wind that tastes of metal.

SERGEANT OKSANA BILYK (30s, goggles) crouches by a concrete shack. LIEUTENANT AUGUSTIN FOURNIER-DIALLO (30s, bandaged hand) checks a map. PRIVATE SOLOMON ADEYEMI (19, rifle) hugs the wall. CORPORAL RUTH TALBOT-KWAN (40s, medic's pack) kneels by the wounded. PRIVATE LIAM O'DWYER-SINGH (20, radio operator) fiddles with a dial. And at the edge of the dust, a lone figure in a tattered coat waves a white rag: ELIAS "THE PRIEST" MANDELBAUM (60s, gaunt, cassock).

BILYK
Hold fire. He's got a flag.

AUGUSTIN
Could be a trick.

SOLOMON
He's not armed.

RUTH
He's barefoot.

LIAM
Sergeant, I'm getting something. Weak.

BILYK
Later. Solomon, cover left.

SOLOMON
Covering.

The Priest shuffles closer, hands raised, rag fluttering.

ELIAS
Please. Don't shoot. I'm only a priest.

AUGUSTIN
Prove it.

ELIAS
I have a Bible in my coat.

RUTH
That proves nothing.

ELIAS
I have bread in my other coat.

LIAM
Bread?

ELIAS
Stale. But bread.

BILYK
Elias, was it? Where are the others?

ELIAS
There are no others. Everyone left in the night.

AUGUSTIN
Everyone?

ELIAS
Both armies.

They stare at him. Silence. Liam taps the radio.

LIAM
Sergeant. It's an order. Cease-fire, effective oh-six-hundred.

BILYK
What time is it now?

AUGUSTIN
Oh-six-ten.

Bilyk lowers her rifle. Solomon lets his drop. Ruth sits down in the dust, laughing quietly. Elias hands the bread to the nearest soldier, who takes it without a word.

BILYK
Pack up.
